course: dictionary
lesson: 2176
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around it. Look for clues about people, machines, or how the word first came into use. «Corruption» is one of these words.
explain: The first meaning is about people with power. When leaders or officials take bribes or use public money for themselves, that is corruption. «The 1990s in independent Ukraine brought hyperinflation, closed factories, poverty and corruption.» The words around it, poverty and closed factories, show that corruption is a bad thing that hurts people.
explain: The second meaning is about damage. A computer file can suffer corruption, which means its data is spoiled, so it will not open. The third meaning is about words. «Ta» is a corruption of «thank you», which means it is a shorter, changed form of the older word. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Corruption means dishonest or illegal behaviour by people with power, such as taking bribes.
fact: «Fight corruption» means to work against dishonest behaviour by people in power.
fact: People can be «accused of corruption» when someone says they have behaved dishonestly, but they are not yet proven guilty.
fact: Corruption can also mean making something bad or rotten, such as «corruption of a computer file», where the data is damaged.
fact: A corruption of a word is a changed form, such as «ta» from «thank you».
exercise: «The 1990s in independent Ukraine brought hyperinflation, closed factories, poverty and corruption.» What does corruption mean here? | *Dishonest behaviour by people with power, such as taking bribes | A very fast way to travel | A happy and peaceful time for all | Lots of new factories being built
exercise: Mia's homework file will not open. The computer says «corruption». What does this mean? | Someone has paid a bribe to the computer | The file has been stolen by a thief | The file has been written on paper | *The data inside is damaged and will not open
exercise: «"Ta" is a corruption of "thank you".» What is the older, proper form? | *thank you | tea | tap | tall
test: In a news story, people say, «The mayor was accused of corruption.» What is the best meaning? | The mayor has lost her voice | *The mayor may have behaved dishonestly, using power for money or gain | The mayor has been very kind to the town | The mayor is bored of her job
test: A character in a story starts out kind but takes bribes and breaks the trust of the people. What does this show? | Corruption in the sense of an old word changing its form | *Corruption, as the character turns bad | A happy ending with no problems | Corruption, as the character becomes a computer file
exam: «Read this: "Citizens want leaders to fight corruption. A file corruption can stop a computer working, and «ta» is a corruption of «thank you».» Which meaning of corruption is used in the first sentence? | Damage to computer data | Changing a word over time | Making a word shorter | *Dishonest behaviour by people with power
